From: SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>
Date: Sun, 02 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] users: add per-user passwordless administration

Add a checkbox to the Users KCM that enables passwordless administrative
actions for an administrator account.  The change is applied by a small
pkexec helper that manages a dedicated group, a sudoers drop-in and a polkit
rule.  The helper is separate from the KCM so the KCM never edits system
security files directly.

This is intentionally opt-in and per-user.  The UI and the helper only allow
accounts in the sudo group.  A contextual help button explains that any
program run by the user can obtain administrator privileges.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
---
